note('Author page 22; archive number 40. The opening displays are numbered (75) and (75′), repeating the preceding scan’s (75); the last number is overwritten and remains 79|78. The page develops expressions for β′ and σ∞(β′), cancels an initial formulation of the norm condition, then compares that condition with the analogous one for β1=σ∞(β′)^{-1}. The interlinear qualification reads “sans supposer vérifiée (*)”. Its star is a reference within the qualification, not a separate equation label. Under the stated involutive action, N(b)=bσ(b)=1 is invariant under b↦σ(b) and b↦b^{-1}; with b1=σ(b)^{-1}, N(b1)=1 is equivalent to N(b)=1 and implies b1=b. This is a targeted group calculation, not a proof of the entire parametrisation. The cancelled α′ under the brace and the joining word between substitutions remain uncertain. The last sentence continues on scan 042; H’s editorial claim that the continuation is outside the lot is disregarded.')
